<title>USA: TABLE - Freddie Mac Q2 net increases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Freddie Mac Q2 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>MCLEAN, Va. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended	    Six Months Ended</p>
<p>			Jun 30,  Mar 31,  Jun 30,  Jun 30,  Jun 30,</p>
<p>			  1997	1997     1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Revenues		 806	777	729    1,583    1,438</p>
<p>Provision for mortgage losses</p>
<p>			   (80)     (80)     (80)    (160)    (160)</p>
<p>Income before extraordinary</p>
<p>item, net of taxes</p>
<p>			    340	329	324	669	625</p>
<p>Extraordinary loss on retirement of debt, net of taxes</p>
<p>				0	  0     (15)	  0     (15)</p>
<p> Net income	     340	329	309	669	610</p>
<p>Preferred stock dividends</p>
<p>			   (26)     (24)     (18)     (50)     (34)</p>
<p>Net income available to common stockholders</p>
<p>			$314	$305	 $291     $619     $576</p>
<p>Operating share (Earnings per common share before</p>
<p>extraordinary item)</p>
<p>			   0.46     0.44     0.43     0.90     0.83</p>
<p>Earnings per commons share</p>
<p>			   0.46     0.44     0.41     0.90     0.81</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>(thousands)</p>
<p>			688,017  691,434  712,913  689,716  713,283</p>
<p>		(dollars in millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp said its per share amounts and weighted shares outstanding reflect a four-for-one stock split effective December 31.</p>
<p>Net income available to common shareholders was calculated before the payment of preferred dividends, earnings per share were calculated after the payment of preferred dividends.</p>
<p>Net income for the second quarter of 1996 included a pre-tax gain of $21 million from the sale of Freddie Mac PCs from the retained portfolio.</p>
<p>The company said total second quarter 1997 charge-offs were $79 million, a decrease of $6 million from second quarter 1996.</p>
